# Frontend conventions

- Use semantic HTML before ARIA.
- Interactive elements must be reachable by keyboard and have visible focus.
- Use `aria-live` for meaningful asynchronous status updates when appropriate.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Use mobile-first Tailwind classes; add breakpoint modifiers only for larger layouts.
- Prefer composition over large prop-driven conditional components.
- Keep data fetching and transport logic separated from visual primitives when remote data is introduced.
- Every remote-data component must make loading, error, empty, and success behavior understandable.
